<section class="featured-publication">
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/743c9ba8-5fb0-4e08-998e-d3066f389141/2027-budget-suggestions-cover.png?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.png" alt="Cover of 2027 Budget Suggestions" title="Cover of 2027 Budget Suggestions" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>2027 Budget Suggestions</h3>
                    <div>Budget Suggestions has the latest information about things that might impact your city or county budget, including state shared revenue distributions, new legislation, economic trends, budget procedures, and more.&nbsp;<em>Published July 2026</em>.</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/cdac7a25-f0ca-4f53-8dae-07706a92f11c/2027-budget-suggestions.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/E81B1094-BDC1-4BEC-AB39-EAFA40140516/annex14cover" alt="Cover of Annexation by Washington Cities and Towns" title="Cover of Annexation by Washington Cities and Towns" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Annexation by Washington Cities and Towns</h3>
                    <div>This publication provides an in-depth review of annexation of territory by Washington cities and towns, including pros and cons, the consequences and impacts of annexation, and the various annexation methods. <em>Published June 2020.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/f7797a3e-d87b-4875-b70a-229a082d7ef3/Annexation-By-Washington-Cities-And-Towns.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/fc83aed8-f9fb-4d4a-bf1c-9d8a971728bb/city-bidding-book-cover.png?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.png" alt="Cover of City Bidding Book - Washington State" title="Cover of City Bidding Book - Washington State" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>City Bidding Book - Washington State</h3>
                    <div>Discusses general competitive bidding requirements for city and town purchases, services, and public works contracts, including the bidding process and potential exemptions. <em>Revised November 2025.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/5f218416-8d03-4ab2-b1af-eb86e42b3e87/City-Bidding-Book-Washington-State.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/bb022073-9e04-48db-bfa2-6764b0fbe040/closest-governments-to-the-people-cover-small.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Closest Governments to the People" title="Cover of Closest Governments to the People" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Closest Governments to the People</h3>
                    <div>This publication, written by Steve Lundin and edited by the Washington State University Division of Governmental Studies and Services, is a comprehensive general reference and resource guide to the complex and varied systems of local governments in Washington State. Topics covered include the historical development of local governments, home rule, local government finance, and the local judiciary. <em>Revised 2015</em>.</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/1c25ae05-968c-4edd-8039-af0cf958baa7/Closest-Governments-To-The-People.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/7A5AC5C7-7694-49C0-8109-AA91E6CF4822/PublicID5" alt="Cover of Code City Handbook" title="Cover of Code City Handbook" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Code City Handbook</h3>
                    <div>Provides essential information for code city officials and incites their powers, duties, and alternatives that are available under the applicable forms of municipal government. <em>Published June 2009.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/f96b74ab-a955-44be-8db2-8fbce16075ea/Code-City-Handbook.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/e74940e0-1058-4df1-8715-80aecd5925aa/conservation-district-handbook-preview.png?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.png" alt="Cover of Conservation District Handbook - Guidelines for Purchasing, Bidding, and Contracting in Washington State Districts" title="Cover of Conservation District Handbook - Guidelines for Purchasing, Bidding, and Contracting in Washington State Districts" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Conservation District Handbook - Guidelines for Purchasing, Bidding, and Contracting in Washington State Districts</h3>
                    <div>Includes general guidance for procuring goods, services, and public works for conservation districts, as well as prevailing wage considerations unique to such districts.&nbsp;<em>Revised October 2025</em>.</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/80dbda97-e5c5-42e8-ad63-c364747cae6e/Conservation-District-Handbook.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/E793AFBC-3041-48A0-81F2-50E70049B30F/PublicID6" alt="Cover of Contracting for Services - Guidelines for Local Governments in Washington State" title="Cover of Contracting for Services - Guidelines for Local Governments in Washington State" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Contracting for Services - Guidelines for Local Governments in Washington State</h3>
                    <div>Provides guidance to local government agencies on contracting for professional architectural and engineering (A&amp;E) services, purchased services, and personal services/consultants. <em>Revised March 2024.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/a79caaa4-f96f-4f2b-8a5f-5e0f4afe3bde/Contracting-For-Services.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/5cab35af-fc5e-4d89-9709-0dacc935ccdf/County-Bidding-Book_preview.png?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.png" alt="Cover of County Bidding Book - Washington State" title="Cover of County Bidding Book - Washington State" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>County Bidding Book - Washington State</h3>
                    <div>Discusses general competitive bidding requirements for county purchases, services, and public works contracts, including the bidding process and potential exemptions.&nbsp;<em>Revised June 2026.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/c216867d-cfcb-48db-8c13-2098a3a5c846/County-Bidding-Book.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/5ffebc22-89e3-4104-92e5-f22e8a4e96c2/County-Commissioner-Guide-cover.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of County Commissioner Guide" title="Cover of County Commissioner Guide" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>County Commissioner Guide</h3>
                    <div>Overview of county government in Washington State and specifically the role of the county commissioners and county councilmembers within county government. It covers key legal doctrines, such as the Public Records Act and the Open Public Meetings Act. <em>Revised February 2025</em>.</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/6134275f-ca98-45b2-8c4c-aa49515363ab/County-Commissioner-Guide.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/07266520-28ad-4ff2-9b43-6cd8f2001666/Homelessness-And-Housing-Toolkit-For-Cities-Cover.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Homelessness and Housing Toolkit for Cities" title="Cover of Homelessness and Housing Toolkit for Cities" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Homelessness and Housing Toolkit for Cities</h3>
                    <div>Provides real-world examples of tools and actions Washington cities have used in responding to the issues of homelessness and affordable housing, including articles on housing levies, tenant protections, and more. Created in partnership with AWC. <em>Revised July 2026.</em><br />
&nbsp;</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/4785af3e-35c7-42ef-8e8e-a44c8d0786c4/Homelessness-And-Housing-Toolkit-For-Cities.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/529D965D-0A9B-48F3-8CBF-59A05C5E399F/irg14" alt="Cover of Initiative and Referendum Guide for Washington Cities and Charter Counties" title="Cover of Initiative and Referendum Guide for Washington Cities and Charter Counties" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Initiative and Referendum Guide for Washington Cities and Charter Counties</h3>
                    <div>Reviews the powers of initiative and referendum as they are exercised in cities and charter counties in Washington. It includes information on how to adopt these powers and which types of municipal activities are subject to these powers. <em>Revised June 2024.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/18593ba0-fa89-4776-84dc-3dcab86b3449/Initiative-And-Referendum-Guide.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/b37973f4-b116-48a8-902e-34b19f0efbb0/knowing-the-territory-cover.jpg?width=225&amp;height=291&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Knowing the Territory - Basic Legal Guidelines for Washington City, County and Special District Officials" title="Cover of Knowing the Territory - Basic Legal Guidelines for Washington City, County and Special District Officials" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Knowing the Territory - Basic Legal Guidelines for Washington City, County and Special District Officials</h3>
                    <div>Describes how local officials can keep out of legal trouble, including information on roles and responsibilities, conflicts of interest, Open Public Meetings Act, Public Records Act, Appearance of Fairness Doctrine, use of public funds, and more. Revised <em>October 2025</em>.</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/1e641718-94a0-408b-b9d9-42b2e1d8180d/Knowing-The-Territory.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/69CA278A-2AC3-471A-B9E0-09E5B50AB353/PublicID23" alt="Cover of Local and Road Improvement Districts Manual for Washington State" title="Cover of Local and Road Improvement Districts Manual for Washington State" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Local and Road Improvement Districts Manual for Washington State</h3>
                    <div>Detailed overview of local improvement district (LID) and road improvement district (RID) procedures, from initiating the LID/RID all the way to the conclusion of financing. <em>Published October 2009.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/4233f39b-f38b-4766-8c22-a0f0d9340d91/Local-And-Road-Improvement-Districts-Manual.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/9B82F31C-DC67-493A-83A2-FC34354842CA/localord14_cover" alt="Cover of Local Ordinances for Washington Cities and Counties" title="Cover of Local Ordinances for Washington Cities and Counties" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Local Ordinances for Washington Cities and Counties</h3>
                    <div>This report has been prepared to assist Washington county, city, and town officials in the drafting and adoption of ordinances, resolutions, motions, and related devices. <em>Revised September 2015.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/44e20d0f-a536-473f-baac-bd7504323330/Local-Ordinances-For-Washington-Cities-And-Counties.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/3658ba02-3c77-4e74-8c57-a3cb3cf9e0f4/Mayor-And-Councilmember-Handbook-cover.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Mayor and Councilmember Handbook" title="Cover of Mayor and Councilmember Handbook" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Mayor and Councilmember Handbook</h3>
                    <div>Reference guide for mayors and city councilmembers. Covers city council meetings, resolving and preventing conflict, budget basics, parliamentary procedures, Open Public Meetings Act, Appearance of Fairness Doctrine, citizen participation, and more.&nbsp;<em>Revised October 2025.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/034f13b6-7ec2-4594-b60b-efaf61dd7d10/Mayor-And-Councilmember-Handbook.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/3E927D50-6CE5-4434-9537-1B2FA35DB20D/opma14cover" alt="Cover of Open Public Meetings Act" title="Cover of Open Public Meetings Act" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Open Public Meetings Act</h3>
                    <div>This publication covers in detail who is subject to the Open Public Meetings Act (OPMA), procedural requirements, executive sessions, exemptions, and penalties, and identifies relevant case law and attorney general opinions. <em>Revised July 2024.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/275e74fc-9d43-4868-8987-a626ad2cea9f/Open-Public-Meetings-Act.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/AE46EA6A-ACEC-452F-9219-5971C90A0CA9/PublicID17" alt="Cover of Personal Services Contracting Manual for Washington Ports" title="Cover of Personal Services Contracting Manual for Washington Ports" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Personal Services Contracting Manual for Washington Ports</h3>
                    <div>In 2008, the Washington State Legislature adopted legislation (codified primarily in Chapter 53.19 RCW) designed to improve public contracting for port districts. <em>Published January 2009.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/a3efe8d5-668a-4b2f-9f1d-ed298b9b6221/Personal-Services-Contracting-Manual-For-Washington-Ports.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/bc50a89f-91e6-4af8-ab46-d71f79fc2fc3/pra-tech-guide-cover_225x291.jpg?width=225&amp;height=291&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of PRA and Records Management Technology Guide" title="Cover of PRA and Records Management Technology Guide" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>PRA and Records Management Technology Guide</h3>
                    <div><p>This guide,&nbsp;created in partnership with the&nbsp;State Auditor&rsquo;s Office Center for Government Innovation, is intended to help Washington government agencies to identify, evaluate, and select records management technology solutions that are best matched with their needs, goals, and budgets. Offers key questions to consider before purchasing records management software, an overview of software options, including descriptions of selected software, and more! <em>Published March 2019</em>.</p>
</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/52d4da6e-1632-4314-8467-dbaaab50cc54/PRA-Tech-Guide.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/93fa1c1a-cef6-48a6-bc27-5f7cbc8bb095/pracover.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Public Records Act for Washington Cities, Counties, and Special Purpose Districts" title="Cover of Public Records Act for Washington Cities, Counties, and Special Purpose Districts" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Public Records Act for Washington Cities, Counties, and Special Purpose Districts</h3>
                    <div>This publication is a comprehensive guide to Washington&rsquo;s Public Records Act requirements, defining public records and agency responsibilities for compliance. It details how to process requests, manage exemptions, deliver records efficiently, and more. <em>Published December 2025.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/796a2402-9ad4-4bde-a221-0d6814ef6edc/Public-Records-Act.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/df61d0ae-854f-4f04-ab50-9560b100acad/Public-Works-Contracting-cover.png?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.png" alt="Cover of Public Works Contracting Best Practices" title="Cover of Public Works Contracting Best Practices" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Public Works Contracting Best Practices</h3>
                    <div>Detailed publication provides helpful tips for public works contracting, focused primarily on the traditional design-bid-build model. Addresses ethics, competition, bid documents, contract award and administration, potential pitfalls, and more. <em>Published June 2023</em>.</div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/386496e5-8d92-402b-a805-1777e6f8b2b5/Public-Works-Contracting.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/1ef88c85-1914-46e7-b43a-79c7dca6a9b3/revenue-guide-cover-city.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Revenue Guide for Washington Cities and Towns" title="Cover of Revenue Guide for Washington Cities and Towns" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Revenue Guide for Washington Cities and Towns</h3>
                    <div>Detailed and up-to-date information on most of the revenue sources available to cities and towns, including property taxes, sales taxes, B&amp;O taxes, lodging taxes, REET, and much more.&nbsp;<em>Revised April 2026.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/d3f7f211-fc63-4b7a-b362-cb17993d5fe5/Revenue-Guide-For-Washington-Cities-And-Towns.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row publication-list-item mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-2 col-12">
                    <img class="img-fluid" src="/getmedia/37df6cdd-f4bd-4cdf-9b58-695f17f51a43/revenue-guide-cover-county.jpg?width=200&amp;height=259&amp;ext=.jpg" alt="Cover of Revenue Guide for Washington Counties" title="Cover of Revenue Guide for Washington Counties" />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-10 col-12">
                    <h3>Revenue Guide for Washington Counties</h3>
                    <div>Detailed and up-to-date information on most of the revenue sources available to counties, including property taxes, sales taxes, lodging taxes, REET, and much more.&nbsp;<em>Revised April 2026.</em></div>
                        <p><a href="/getmedia/4865001b-1f63-410a-a5ed-8d1ad8d752f3/Revenue-Guide-For-Washington-Counties.pdf?ext=.pdf">View/download this publication in Adobe Acrobat (PDF)</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>

</section>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>

    </div>
    
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row back-to-top-container">
            <div class="col">
